# WSL Test Execution

When the workspace runs under WSL:

- Never run full, batch, directory-wide, repeated, parallel, or repository-wide test suites.
- Run one narrowly targeted test file, test case, or filter at a time.
- Run test commands sequentially and wait for each command to finish.
- Do not use repetition loops for race tests.
- Prefer the smallest command that proves the changed behavior.
- Ask the user before expanding test scope beyond a single targeted file or filter.
- Apply the same restriction to subagents and include it explicitly in every implementation or review prompt.
